{
  "dom_id": "step-q69510",
  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14212914/assets/4b441f7b59f59240141380711d5d380ea58cafa01f8a288f1e5c8bc7685650cf.png)\n\nConsider the diagram shown above, where $\\overset{\\to }{PS}=a,$ $\\overset{\\to }{SQ}=b,$ and $\\overset{\\to }{PT}=c.$ Find $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ in terms of $a,b$ and $c.$",
  "worked_solution": "We want to find a \"path\" from $P$ to $Q$ consisting only of the vectors $a,b,$ and $c.$\n\nAccording to the triangle law of addition,\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{PQ}=\\overset{\\to }{PS}+\\overset{\\to }{SQ}\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14212914/assets/1bf9ce3f20027a3ce358f8a0a9d72107f087021ca698e677df367e05a7c3e5bb.png)\n\nNow, from the original diagram, we have that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{PS}=a,\\,\\overset{\\to }{SQ}=b.\n$$\n\nLet's add these to our diagram.\n\n \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14212914/assets/6b37dcafa2b2b913d7e5328e19257c4d873c5877186df24626033fec8216da05.png)\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =\\overset{\\to }{PS}+\\overset{\\to }{SQ} \\\\  & =a+b\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
